    "slug": "somali-president-recognizes-finance-and-foreign-affairs-ministries-for-top-performance-in-2026",
    "summary": "On September 13, 2026, President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud presented awards to the Ministries of Finance and Foreign Affairs for their outstanding performance in 2026. The ceremony in Mogadishu highlighted the ministries' achievements against set targets.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud attended a ceremony in Mogadishu on September 13, 2026, where the performance results of federal government ministries were announced. The evaluation assessed how well each ministry met its plans and targets for the year 2026. The Ministries of Finance and Foreign Affairs received the highest rankings and were awarded plaques in recognition of their strong performance.\n\nThe event underscored the government's focus on accountability and results-driven governance. By publicly evaluating ministries, the administration aims to encourage efficiency and transparency across all sectors. This is part of broader efforts to improve public service delivery and meet the expectations of Somali citizens.\n\nThe Ministry of Finance has been central to Somalia's economic reforms, including managing the national budget and engaging with international financial institutions. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs has played a key role in strengthening Somalia's diplomatic ties and attracting international support for development and security initiatives.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these recognitions highlight progress in key areas that directly affect remittances, investment, and Somalia's global standing. A well-performing finance ministry can enhance economic stability, while an effective foreign ministry can foster better relations with countries where many Somalis reside, potentially easing travel and consular services.\n\nThe awards also serve as a signal to international partners that the government is committed to good governance, which could lead to increased support for reconstruction and development projects. The diaspora often contributes significantly to such efforts and may view these developments as positive indicators for future engagement.\n\nPresident Hassan Sheikh Mohamud's participation reflects the administration's emphasis on merit-based recognition within the government. The ceremony concluded with the president urging all ministries to maintain and improve their performance in the coming year.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/09/13/maaliyadda-iyo-arrimaha-dibadda-oo-ku-guuleystay-qiimeynta-waxqabadka/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=maaliyadda-iyo-arrimaha-dibadda-oo-ku-guuleystay-qiimeynta-waxqabadka",
