    "content": "The Towfiiq political party, led by Sheikh Mohamed Shakir Ali Hassan, has been officially barred from participating in the run-off election in Galmudug, Horseed Media reported. The decision excludes the party from the next phase of the electoral process in the central Somali region.\n\nGalmudug has been conducting elections for its regional parliament and president. The run-off election is typically held when no candidate secures an outright majority in the initial round. The exclusion of Towfiiq comes amid ongoing disputes over the electoral process in the region.\n\nSheikh Mohamed Shakir Ali Hassan is a prominent religious and political figure in Galmudug. His party's exclusion may further intensify political tensions in the region, which has faced repeated delays and disagreements over election procedures.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, developments in Galmudug are closely followed, as many diaspora members maintain familial and business ties to the region. A stable and inclusive electoral process is seen as crucial for the region's development. The exclusion of a major party could undermine confidence in the election's credibility among diaspora observers.\n\nIt remains unclear what specific reasons led to Towfiiq's exclusion or whether the party will challenge the decision. The regional electoral commission has not issued a detailed statement. Horseed Media reported the exclusion but did not provide further details.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/urur-siyaasadeedka-towfiiq-oo-si-rasmi-ah-looga-saaray-loolanka-doorashada-galmudug/425652/",
