    "content": "The Somali National Army (SNA) announced that its forces, together with the Gorgor commando brigade, have captured the town of Geel-gub and several strategic bases in the Middle Shabelle region. The operation involved the 18th Gorgor Commando Battalion, the 12th Special Forces Gorgor Battalion, and the 3rd SNA Battalion. State media reported that government troops now have full control of Geel-gub and surrounding positions. However, not all of the seized bases were named.\n\nThe operation was conducted jointly by the different units, according to military officials. They stated that the forces operated in the town and its outskirts. This development marks another step in the ongoing military campaign against Al-Shabaab in the region.\n\nMiddle Shabelle has been a focal point of recent security operations as the federal government seeks to push Al-Shabaab out of key population centers and rural strongholds. The Gorgor commandos, trained for counter-insurgency missions, have played a leading role in these efforts. The capture of Geel-gub could disrupt militant movements and supply routes in the area.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this news holds particular significance. Many diaspora members maintain close ties to families in Middle Shabelle and have invested in local businesses and properties. Stability in the region is essential for diaspora-funded development projects and for the safe return of those who wish to visit or invest. Additionally, the success of Somali-led operations reinforces confidence in the national security forces, a key concern for diaspora communities that support rebuilding efforts.\n\nWhile the full details of the operation remain undisclosed, the government's claim of territorial gains reflects its continued commitment to restoring state authority. The international community, including diaspora organizations, often monitors such developments as indicators of progress in Somalia's security sector. The coming weeks will reveal whether these gains are sustained and expanded.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/13/kumaandooska-gorgor-oo-sheegay-inuu-la-wareegay-geel-gub-iyo-saldhigyo-ku-dhow/",
